  "semantics": "Line 1: n m w (1<=n<=1000, 0<=m<=min(n(n-1)/2,10^5), 1<=w<=1000); line 2: n weights 1..1000; line 3: n beauties 1..10^6; then m lines x y (1<=x,y<=n, x!=y, all pairs distinct). Friendship groups are connected components; from each group invite all of it, exactly one member, or nobody. Print the unique maximum total beauty with total weight <= w (0 when nothing fits; at most 1000*10^6 = 10^9). Oracle: union-find components plus grouped knapsack over capacities in O((n+groups)*w); checked against subset enumeration with transitive-closure groups, per-group option enumeration, and a sparse exact-weight DP.",
  "interpretationNotes": [
    "Friendship pairs are treated as unordered: a pair and its reverse are rejected together as duplicates (m <= n(n-1)/2 only makes sense for unordered pairs); a lone reversed pair is valid.",
    "Unique scalar output; stdio; no checker needed (generated_checker is null); not interactive, no floating point, no multiple valid outputs.",
    "Parser requires exactly 3 + m non-empty lines (LF or CRLF, optional final newline), canonical decimal integers without sign/leading zeros."
  ],
